Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 19:23:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Let Ctrl+C quit while only the TUI tools server starts, and
 show MCP startup

The TUI starts its own codex_tui MCP server for every thread, and the chat widget
counted that startup as running work. A Ctrl+C in the first fraction of a second after
launch therefore interrupted the startup instead of quitting, left the TUI's own tools
uninitialized and added an "MCP startup interrupted" warning. Nothing on screen showed
why, because the status indicator stayed hidden during MCP startup.

An MCP startup round now marks the TUI busy only while it waits for more than the
TUI tools server. That server no longer appears in the "Booting MCP server" header,
and Ctrl+C quits while it is all that is starting. While user MCP servers start, the
status indicator shows the header, so Ctrl+C visibly interrupts their startup.
